ion":"zstd","level":3,"row_group_size":65536,"version":"2.6"},"pyarrow":"23.0.1","subset_policy":"all committed format rules for seven countries; first 32 distinct codes plus named examples; all registration units and one entity association per code","world_source_rows":144675},"notices":{"DATASET_CARD.md":"# Thereabouts golden v2\n\nVerified country-checkpointed city normalization at H3 resolution 8.\n6,875,329 places; 68,923 absorbing cities/towns; 66,226,680 compact cells.\n\nCountry/state/land membership retains the base snapshot. Policy polygons, accepted city polygons, GHSL urban allocation and optional town radii precede rural polygons/nearest settlements. Nearest answers beyond 25 km are flagged; 50 km remains the inclusive cutoff.\n\nSee quality.json and quality/<country>.json for regenerated checks, including failures; these consistency/source checks are not independent accuracy. Dhaka has an inferred urban allocation, not a verified municipal boundary. See docs/GOLDEN_V2.md for reproduction and limitations.\n","DATA_LICENSES.md":"# Golden dataset attribution and licence summary (draft)\n\nKeep every row's original licence and provenance. This is a combined derivative\ndatabase, not a relicensing of its inputs. Review distribution obligations before\npublishing this draft, including attribution and database share-alike terms.\n\n| Input | Recorded terms / required attribution |\n| --- | --- |\n| OpenStreetMap land | ODbL 1.0; © OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright |\n| Overture divisions | ODbL 1.0; Overture Maps Foundation, OpenStreetMap and the upstream sources retained in provenance |\n| GeoNames places and postal | CC BY 4.0; GeoNames, https://www.geonames.org/; GB postal also retains Royal Mail copyright/database-right 2022 |\n| geoBoundaries | Per-layer licences in reconciliation provenance; the policy only admits its explicit compatible-licence list |\n| Country / subdivision codes | DataHub PDDL 1.0; GeoNames CC BY 4.0; iso-codes/pycountry LGPL 2.1 or later |\n| OurAirports | Public domain; https://ourairports.com/data/ |\n| UN/LOCODE | UNECE / DataHub, PDDL 1.0; source identifies edition 2024.2.0 |\n| Timezones | timezone-boundary-builder and OpenStreetMap, ODbL 1.0; IANA tables public domain |\n| Phone | Google libphonenumber, Apache 2.0 |\n| DB-IP Lite | CC BY 4.0; “IP Geolocation by DB-IP”, https://db-ip.com |\n\nSource URLs, releases, original notices, identity and boundary evidence remain\nin the acquired manifests, reconciled partitions and golden provenance columns.\n\n## GHSL\n\nCC BY 4.0. European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC), GHS-UCDB R2024A; Pesaresi et al. (2024), Advances on the Global Human Settlement Layer by joint assessment of Earth Observation and population survey data, International Journal of Digital Earth 17(1). https://doi.org/10.1080/17538947.2024.2390454\n\nhttps://human-settlement.emergency.copernicus.eu/GHSLhowToCite.php\nWGS84 conversion and city allocation are modifications.\n"},"sources":["plate source tables and committed plate-country policies"]},"writer":"0.3.0"},"sources":["plate source tables and committed plate-country policies"],"attribution":"Plate sources retain per-row licenses; see golden notices and format provenance","files":[{"path":"plate_formats-00000.bin","kind":"plate_formats","size":1770,"sha256":"13d9a80c75551ee7ea04aef1db5d45b10125c6a3bdce540db4afb1d2ead96985"},{"path":"plate_format_evidence-00000.bin","kind":"plate_format_evidence","size":196,"sha256":"53de4bc8c26046937c8d264efbcd627769b3a6932c03f9742353a7fef0cfcffc"},{"path":"plate_codes-00000.bin","kind":"plate_codes","size":1298,"sha256":"d433a23380fa64a2c22b19bea55449af9ff11531b64975e9ed5845abcad71158"},{"path":"plate_code_evidence-00000.bin","kind":"plate_code_evidence","size":256,"sha256":"f7898c2800388bc41fcf5b378e8639396289ed44c2735f94d5134fac74bb7446"},{"path":"plate_priors-00000.bin","kind":"plate_priors","size":96,"sha256":"5bbf3716af4784f8efbfc8b3ab829b3